  "tasks": [
    {
      "id": "attempt-evidence-envelope-0143",
      "title": "Prepare a lossless synthetic attempt envelope for failed and unparseable responses",
      "role": "benchmark",
      "model": "default",
      "effort": "high",
      "blocked_by": [],
      "limits": {"timeout_minutes": 90, "max_turns": 65},
      "exports": [{"source": "reports", "sessions": [656]}],
      "body": "## Goal\nClose one preparation gap: the old synthetic run-record contract cannot retain truly empty or malformed responses as valid records. First report and preserve the compatibility measurement, then prepare a separate, explicitly synthetic attempt/evidence envelope and data-only rehearsal. Expected gain: benchmark/attempt-evidence-0143.md and its JSON/checker demonstrate lossless retention of every planned slot and attempt independently of response parsing; a later independent reviewer can check this bounded contract. This is benchmark preparation, not product implementation or real-run admission. No session can run LabVIEW.\n## Acceptance\n- [ ] Inspect .session/exports/manifest.json and exported #656 report; record availability and identities. Pin current commit, relevant source hashes and normative pointers. Before changing files, save .session/artifacts/attempt-compatibility-0143.json with the observed old-validator outcomes for intact, empty and malformed/truncated interrupted responses, and the exact unsupported representation boundary. Inspect helpers before execution; use only the current bounded checker or selected validation helpers, never historical builders/main/check/evaluator. Do not repeat the closed grouping review or assert historical independence.\n- [ ] Create only benchmark/attempt-evidence-0143.md, benchmark/attempt-evidence-0143.json and benchmark/verify_attempt_evidence_0143.py. Define a separately versioned synthetic-only envelope derived from /future_extension and /binding_design in project-run-binding-0138.json. Keep existing record/manifest schemas, eight mandatory nulls/reasons, legacy validators, accepted grouping package, keys and preparation index unchanged. Preserve plan slot identity, comparison/repetition mapping, unique attempt identity and explicit attempt order without treating repetitions as retries. Missing slots and retained attempts must remain distinguishable. Declare unsupported real policies explicitly; no retry/selection/stopping policy is authorized.\n- [ ] Retain exact request/response/error bytes, including zero bytes, invalid UTF-8 and malformed/truncated JSON, with unambiguous encoding, byte size and SHA256. Preserve independently readable original payloads; never manufacture a parseable replacement or silently discard failed attempts. Distinguish response absent from response present with zero bytes, and parsing/legacy-record availability from transport/attempt outcome. Evidence entries bind object identity, producer/version, UTC/attempt identity and verification status; local byte consistency cannot become trusted provider/storage/isolation authority. Synthetic data and unavailable actual authority must be explicit.\n- [ ] Save expected decisions and accounting in the repository JSON before executing the new rehearsal. Cover positive intact records, empty/malformed/binary responses, interrupted/failed/missing arms, retained failed attempts followed by another attempt, duplicate attempt identity/order, mismatched slot/group/repetition, omitted required evidence, corrupt payload/hash/size/encoding and fabricated verification/admission labels. A retry inventory is not permission to retry or select a successful result. Unresolved attempt selection, failed or missing arms and unavailable trusted evidence cannot produce completed real comparisons. Preserve separate planned/present/attempt/parseable/failed/interrupted inventories and separate correctness/grounding denominators; no semantic score is invented. Derive counts from bytes rather than report summaries.\n- [ ] The standard-library repository-only checker validates saved expectations, payload round trips, references, source pins and all inventories without network, prepared environment, session inputs/artifacts or file writes. Read executable dependencies before running them. Demonstrate unchanged legacy behavior and continued success of python3 -I benchmark/verify_project_run_binding_0138.py; preserve its exact scoped bytes. Keep actual admissions, model/reader/native executions, scored runs and semantic passes zero, actual costs unavailable and benchmark_ready=false. An unconditional real-admission block is a scope boundary, not a verified admission algorithm.\n- [ ] Report exact changed files, hashes, commands/results, remaining contract boundaries and the bounded scope for subsequent independent review. Save detailed observations in .session/artifacts/attempt-evidence-results-0143.json. No method acceptance, native validity, product gain, full readiness audit, index promotion, threshold or owner request. If compatibility evidence contradicts the proposed cut, report it before changing the design; preserve useful partial work and name the precise next step.\n## Verification\npython3 -I benchmark/verify_attempt_evidence_0143.py\nThe checker must also verify unchanged source pins and the retained legacy/grouping boundary using inspected helpers or the repository-only grouping checker; no evaluator.\n## Context\nThe shaper read project-run-binding-0138.md: legacy synthetic records require parseable structured responses even for interrupted attempts; its future extension proposes separate attempt/evidence storage. #656 recommends technical F1 CLEAR for grouping at 51e672d06c079105a8d9dec23a0b44dc1c7ac5db, with historical evidence and exposure limits. Close that narrow review; do not reconstruct missing #653 artifacts. The selected remaining gap is lossless failed-attempt retention needed before runner/scorer integration, not a new global readiness inventory. The unsuccessful bounded POC was delivered; benchmark preparation resumed. Whole-method review and explicit owner acceptance still precede product implementation.\n## Budget\nRead docs/perpetua/evaluation.md and docs/perpetua/roles.md; exported report #656 after checking .session/exports/manifest.json. Read benchmark/project-run-binding-0138.md, targeted /future_extension, /binding_design, /pins and relevant rehearsal pointers in its JSON, and the selected checker/helper definitions in benchmark/verify_project_run_binding_0138.py and benchmark/scripts/run_record.py. Read benchmark/baseline/run-record.template.json, benchmark/baseline/run-manifest.template.json and only the attempt/repetition/failure/evidence sections of benchmark/baseline/runner-contract.md and benchmark/project-paired-0136.md. No whole large JSON dumps, binary/base64 dumps, broad history/source searches, original key/C1 review, old builders or evaluator. At most two additional directly linked references for a demonstrated ambiguity. Keep command output short, report the measurement early, and preserve exact source pointers for a cold independent review."
    }
  ]
}

